    "explanation": "To both parties. This was a short metered RydeX trip on 26 August 2026: 4.04 km actually driven, billed at SGD 9.70 against a booked optimal route of 3.20 km. Everything below is read off the trip record (EV-TRIP-02844), the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02844) and the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02844), all of which are complete and carry full weight (1.0).\n\nRider — your claim is partly upheld. The governing distance is the trace figure, as POL-RD-01 requires: it records 4.04 km against the 3.20 km optimal, an excess of 0.84 km, which is 26.25% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass (0.84 km > 0.8 km; 26.25% > 20%), and neither materiality gate is met (0.84 km is not > 8.0 km and 26.25% is not > 50%), so this is an ordinary established deviation, not a material one. The rounded trip-record copy (4.00 km) would give exactly 0.80 km and fail the strict absolute gate; POL-RD-01 forbids citing it for the threshold test. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)–(c): 46 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s. No clause adjusts the 3.20 km baseline — there are no amendments to pickup or dropoff (POL-RD-05 does not run), the vehicle type is RYDE_X not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12 does not run), and the chat log (EV-CHAT-02844) holds 0 messages, so no rider instruction exists to attribute any excess to (POL-RD-04 does not run).\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, run on the booked optimal route: (3.80 + 0.75 × 3.20 + 0.28 × 6.00) × 1.0 surge, the multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier as that clause requires, plus the 0.80 platform fee, plus 0 ERP and tolls on the optimal route, plus no fixed surcharge and no waiting fee, less no promo discount = SGD 8.68. Charged_total is SGD 9.70, so the refund is SGD 1.02, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 1.05. That is above the SGD 0.50 de-minimis floor and about 10.5% of the charge, well short of the 90% that would convert the outcome to a full refund. So the amount returned is SGD 1.05 — not the SGD 2.00 contested and not the SGD 9.70 mentioned in the claim text. Nothing is added for ERP or surcharges: no gantry was crossed, no surcharge applied, and POL-RD-09(1) would in any event forbid stacking off-route ERP on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. The monetary effect (SGD 1.05) is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so it executes on issue under POL-GEN-05.\n\nDriver — your explanation for the longer route, 'one-way streets', cannot be weighed. The only artifact that could test an external traffic cause is the traffic advisory for this trip, and EV-ADVIS-02844-01 is absent: payload null, admissibility status MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, and no advisory covers the Blk 412 Pasir Ris Dr 6 corridor in this window. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08, exactly as POL-RD-13 provides for this pattern: the deviation stands at the measured figure and POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal, and the ruling records that the explanation was discarded and that no advisory was on file. Your advocate's request to escalate under POL-RD-10(5) is declined. POL-RD-13 settles this pattern, and the explanation asserted names no road, no closure, no queue or incident and no advisory identifier; an absence in the bundle is not an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and nothing in POL-RD-03 would have exonerated a one-way-street network even on a complete advisory file. For completeness on the audit trail: the claim put forward on this point was discarded by the referee because it cited the impaired advisory without naming its issue code, which POL-GEN-02(1) requires.\n\nYour remaining points are accepted. Establishment is correctly conceded; POL-RD-06 is not engaged because the deviation is not material, and the profile check fails on its own terms in any event (deviation_flags_90d = 1, below the count of 3, and 1 of 247 completed trips is about 0.4%, below the 5% ratio), so there is no conduct referral — the only fields used for that test are the two POL-GEN-01 permits. The rider's profile does not engage the POL-RD-08 extra-corroboration proviso (deviation_claims_60d = 0). No driver compensation is payable: the billed distance (4.0 km) falls short of the trace distance (4.04 km) by 0.04 km, far under the 1.0 km that POL-RD-04 requires.\n\nOn weight and confidence: the only artifact below full weight is the absent advisory at 0.0, which under POL-GEN-02(3) can carry no fact and is not relied on by this ruling; the facts the ruling rests on — the trace distance, the optimal distance and the charged total — are each carried by artifacts at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and my confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor. No clause produces a referral (POL-RD-06(c), POL-RD-09(4), POL-NS-05(ii) and POL-NS-07 are all unengaged), so the referrals list is empty. This ruling is provisional and either of you may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
